      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 4381,
        "name": "Old Operative's Pocket Watch",
        "desc": "<p>A standard-issue pocket watch given to Fatui Operatives.</p><p>The erosion and oxidation on the casing serve as a loyal record of its owners' days spent as an instrument, enforcing the Fatui's will.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://upload-static.hoyoverse.com/hoyolab-wiki/2023/09/28/35428890/4b2a69696dda03d6e097cc0d57cb870f_6107236721935461974.png"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 4382,
        "name": "Operative's Standard Pocket Watch",
        "desc": "<p>A standard-issue pocket watch given to Fatui Operatives.</p><p>The head of the watch is not well-designed, as the outer casing has way too many sharp angles, which can cause excessive wear and tear on clothes. As such, there will always be those who will stuff this watch into a more practical, less distinctive casing for use.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://upload-static.hoyoverse.com/hoyolab-wiki/2023/09/28/35428890/184c18cb6357e78e1d3e20c47017fe07_4895960214088588064.png"
      },
      {
        "type": "CustomEntry",
        "epId": 4383,
        "name": "Operative's Constancy",
        "desc": "<p>An accessory with a Delusion mounted on it. This is source of the Fatui Operative's power.</p><p>That said, taking it off would not detract from the fact that said Operative has physical abilities far beyond that of ordinary humans, forged through long years of training and combat experience. As for them, they are well-aware that they have sacrificed their past, present, and future upon the altar of the Fatui's ideal paradise, such that the damage they cause themselves on account of using a Delusion's power matters not at all.</p>",
        "iconUrl": "https://upload-static.hoyoverse.com/hoyolab-wiki/2023/09/28/35428890/5e0857060fa4992e7401c359a519848f_8226659171460274523.png"
